    "hero": {
      "title": "🧼 Soap Business Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a soap maker, from Foam Grown to Savonnerie Delaunay."
    },
    "intro": "Good soap business names hint at what's in the bar or how it feels to use: a lather pun, a hedgerow plant, or a French word that sounds like a little shop in Provence. Making cold-process bars for markets, Etsy or a shop of your own? This **soap business name generator** has names in eight styles, from lather puns and cheeky goats to hedgerow naturals and French luxury.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good soap business names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Foam Truths</strong>: a pun on home truths, quick and memorable.</li><li><strong>Clay &amp; Lye</strong>: two soapmaking ingredients: lye is what turns oil into soap.</li><li><strong>Bar Humbug</strong>: a Christmas pun on Scrooge that works all year.</li><li><strong>Muddy Hedgehog Suds</strong>: funny and very British, good for a market stall.</li><li><strong>Honey Duck Soaps</strong>: cute, for children's soaps and gift sets.</li><li><strong>Nettle &amp; Willow</strong>: two native plants, for natural and herbal soaps.</li><li><strong>Maison du Savon</strong>: French for \"house of soap\", for a luxury feel.</li><li><strong>Booth &amp; Sons Soapmakers</strong>: a family name and an old trade word, for a traditional range.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How soap names work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>The words of the craft:</strong> soap is made by saponification, the reaction between oils and lye (sodium hydroxide). <em>Lye</em>, <em>lather</em>, <em>suds</em> and <em>bar</em> all make good name parts.</li><li><strong>French for luxury:</strong> <em>savon</em> is French for soap and a <em>savonnerie</em> is a soap works, which is why French names sound upmarket on a label.</li><li><strong>Plants for natural soap:</strong> herbs and hedgerow names, like <em>Calendula Soap Kitchen</em>, tell people what's inside.</li><li><strong>The rules:</strong> in the UK, soap sold to cleanse the skin is a cosmetic. Before it goes on sale it needs a safety assessment by a qualified assessor, a UK Responsible Person, and notification through the government's Submit Cosmetic Product Notification service. The label lists ingredients by their INCI names.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>A soap name goes on every label, every market banner and your shop, so it's worth a few minutes' checking before anything is printed:</p><ul><li><strong>Press Check</strong> on any name above. The <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a> looks up the domain, links to the company register (Companies House in the UK) and opens the trade mark search and social handles.</li><li><strong>Search where you'll trade.</strong> Look the name up on maps, marketplaces and social media. Two businesses with the same name confuse customers and reviews.</li><li><strong>Check the name doesn't make a claim you can't back up. Cosmetics can't claim to treat or cure conditions, so steer clear of words like <em>Healing</em>.</strong></li></ul><p>This is general guidance, not legal advice. For the full process, from shortlisting to registering, read our guide to <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Tips for soapmakers",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Try it on a small label.</strong> Soap labels are small, so a short name stays readable.</li><li><strong>Think about candles and bath bombs.</strong> <em>Soap Co.</em> is clear, but <em>Bath Co.</em> or <em>Soap &amp; Candle Co.</em> leaves room to grow.</li></ul><p>Related trades: the <a href=\"candle-business-name-generator.html\">Candle</a>, <a href=\"skincare-brand-name-generator.html\">Skincare Brand</a> and <a href=\"makeup-brand-name-generator.html\">Makeup Brand</a> name generators. For a name with no trade attached, try the <a href=\"brand-name-generator.html\">Brand Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_shops-names.html\">shops, brands and makers business name generators</a>.</p>"
